  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 400 AM EDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nOn Monday night, the cold front will finally push southward out of \nthe region. This will allow weak surface high pressure to fill in \nand bring a much-needed reprieve from the uncomfortable heat and \nhumidity that's been felt over the past several days. Per the most \nrecent LREF guidance, lows on Tuesday will be in the upper 60s north \nof the Parkways and around 70 for places south. Conditions will also \nbe dry through early Wednesday as the surface high slowly drifts to \nthe east. Afternoon highs on Tuesday will be in the upper 80s, but \nwith dew points in the mid 60s it will feel very comfortable \noutside. For Tuesday night, expect lows in the mid-to-upper 60s \nacross the region.\n\nA broader pattern shift will begin to take place on Wednesday as the \nupper ridge over the western CONUS begins to amplify and an upper \ntrough over the eastern CONUS digs southward. The southern periphery \nof the upper jet will be placed over southern Indiana and central \nKentucky, acting as a pathway for multiple shortwaves to pass over \nthe region through the start of the weekend. The first shortwave \nwill move into the region Wednesday afternoon, bringing back chances \nfor showers and thunderstorms for the remainder of the week. While \ntemperatures Wednesday afternoon will be in the upper 80s/low 90s, \nthe repeated rounds of convective activity afterwards will keep \ndaytime highs in the low-to-mid 80s for the rest of the forecast \nperiod.\n\nWhile there is some uncertainty in the timing and progression, a \ncold front is expected to move through the area near the end of the \nforecast period (late Friday-Saturday), with surface high pressure \nbuilding in behind. This will provide an end to the repeated rounds \nof showers and storms, with the convective activity pushing off to \nthe south and east. With northerly flow persisting behind the front, \ntemperatures will continue to remain mild, potentially making for a \nrather comfortable weekend ahead.",
